{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '580,765p' src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc | nl -ba -v580\"","aggregated_output":"   580\t\n   581\t(defn- record-last-value\n   582\t  [state state-after value]\n   583\t  (assoc state-after\n   584\t         :last-value value\n   585\t         :last-value-2 (:last-value state)\n   586\t         :last-value-3 (:last-value-2 state)))\n   587\t\n   588\t\n   589\t(defn- finalize-eval\n   590\t  \"Drain the round's output and its result from the output medium.  The\n   591\t   newest result is this round's: the evaluator answers once per halted\n   592\t   program, after its prints.\"\n   593\t  [state state' vm']\n   594\t  (let [[state'' output-text results] (drain-output (assoc state' :vm vm'))]\n   595\t    (if (seq results)\n   596\t      (let [value (peek results)]\n   597\t        [(record-last-value state state'' value)\n   598\t         (str output-text (format-value value))])\n   599\t      [state''\n   600\t       (str output-text \"Error: \" result-loss-text)])))\n   601\t\n   602\t\n   603\t(defn- drain-observer\n   604\t  \"Advance one observer past every batch still on its medium, keeping any\n   605\t   gap it recovers across.  A nil observer — a session without that medium —\n   606\t   stays nil.\"\n   607\t  [observer]\n   608\t  (when observer\n   609\t    (loop [observer observer]\n   610\t      (let [{:keys [status] observer' :observer}\n   611\t            (observer/observe-next observer)]\n   612\t        (if (#{:ok :gap} status) (recur observer') observer')))))\n   613\t\n   614\t\n   615\t(defn- consume-failed-round\n   616\t  \"Answer a round that threw with a recoverable shell state.\n   617\t\n   618\t   The failed input is consumed exactly once: each of the session's\n   619\t   observers resumes from the session the throw carried — the failing\n   620\t   stage's, matched by the medium it holds — or from where the round began\n   621\t   when it carried none, and reads past every batch still on its medium.\n   622\t   The shell is the only appender and appends one batch per round, so what\n   623\t   remains is the failed batch alone.  The VM is the one the round began\n   624\t   with, so a half-run continuation cannot be resumed — and its error\n   625\t   replayed — by the next input.  Output the round already emitted is\n   626\t   drained here, once.\"\n   627\t  [state error]\n   628\t  (let [carried (get-in (ex-data error) [:session :observer])\n   629\t        resume (fn [observer]\n   630\t                 (if (and observer\n   631\t                          carried\n   632\t                          (= (:stream carried) (:stream observer)))\n   633\t                   carried\n   634\t                   observer))\n   635\t        program (drain-observer (resume (:observer state)))\n   636\t        rows (drain-observer (resume (:row-observer state)))\n   637\t        gaps-before (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n   638\t                       (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0))\n   639\t        gaps-after (+ (:ingress-gaps program 0) (:ingress-gaps rows 0))\n   640\t        [state' output-text]\n   641\t        (drain-output\n   642\t          (cond-> (assoc state :observer program :row-observer rows)\n   643\t            (> gaps-after gaps-before)\n   644\t            (assoc :ingress-loss? true)))]\n   645\t    [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))\n   646\t\n   647\t\n   648\t(defn- ingress-gaps\n   649\t  [state]\n   650\t  (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n   651\t     (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0)))\n   652\t\n   653\t\n   654\t(defn- run-expander-stage\n   655\t  \"Drive the expander over `program-in` and drain its summary.  It expands\n   656\t   each observed batch and appends the tree packet to `program-out`; a\n   657\t   failed expansion forwards nothing, yet its cursor advances (yin.vm.macro.md\n   658\t   decision 12).  Returns the state with the expander's progress and the\n   659\t   drained `{:errors :forwarded}` summary.\"\n   660\t  [state]\n   661\t  (let [{:keys [observer consumer]}\n   662\t        (macro/step {:observer (:observer state), :consumer (:expander state)})\n   663\t        [expander summary] (macro/drain-errors consumer)]\n   664\t    [(assoc state :observer observer :expander expander) summary]))\n   665\t\n   666\t\n   667\t(defn- run-evaluator-stage\n   668\t  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n   669\t   expanded tree packet into the VM, runs it, and answers its value on the\n   670\t   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n   671\t   the other.\"\n   672\t  [{:keys [load-program run-program] :as state}]\n   673\t  (let [{:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n   674\t        (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n   675\t                                 :consumer (:vm state)}\n   676\t                                engine/ready-for-ingress?\n   677\t                                load-program\n   678\t                                run-program)]\n   679\t    (assoc state :row-observer observer :vm vm)))\n   680\t\n   681\t\n   682\t(defn- format-expansion-errors\n   683\t  [errors]\n   684\t  (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"Error: Macro expansion failed: \" (format-value %))\n   685\t                      errors)))\n   686\t\n   687\t\n   688\t(defn- run-evaluation\n   689\t  \"The evaluator half of a round whose expander forwarded a program: run\n   690\t   it, then either finalize the value or consume the failure.  `state` is\n   691\t   the round's starting state; `expanded` already carries the expander's\n   692\t   progress, which a failing evaluation keeps.\"\n   693\t  [state expanded]\n   694\t  (try\n   695\t    (let [gaps-before (ingress-gaps expanded)\n   696\t          evaluated (run-evaluator-stage expanded)]\n   697\t      (cond\n   698\t        (> (ingress-gaps evaluated) gaps-before)\n   699\t        [(assoc evaluated :ingress-loss? true)\n   700\t         (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n   701\t\n   702\t        (vm/halted? (:vm evaluated))\n   703\t        (finalize-eval state evaluated\n   704\t                       (engine/restore-initial-env (:env (:vm expanded))\n   705\t                                                   (:vm evaluated)))\n   706\t\n   707\t        :else\n   708\t        (throw\n   709\t          (ex-info\n   710\t            \"Program stream did not form a complete, runnable Yin VM program.\n   711\tHint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n   712\t            {:vm-type (:vm-type state)}))))\n   713\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n   714\t      (consume-failed-round (assoc expanded :vm (:vm state)) error))))\n   715\t\n   716\t\n   717\t(defn- eval-program\n   718\t  \"Evaluate one frontend program — the map AST the compilers emit or a\n   719\t   datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n   720\t   projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n   721\t   declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n   722\t   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the evaluator only when a\n   723\t   program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n   724\t   batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n   725\t   input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n   726\t   is appended.\n   727\t\n   728\t   The observers recover across a gap on their own, but the shell reads the\n   729\t   gap counts around the round: an increase on any medium means one or more\n   730\t   batches were never run, so resuming as though execution were complete\n   731\t   would report a result built on programs the VM never saw.  The loss is\n   732\t   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset